{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01648",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.69,
      "end_seconds": 4.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.93,
      "end_seconds": 11.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "so, you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.11,
      "end_seconds": 21.26,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "I mean, I wanted to get a fall and pain in my left hip looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.96,
      "end_seconds": 25.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.07,
      "end_seconds": 36.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "let me think, I've had it for six months my neighbour said I should get it looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.93,
      "end_seconds": 39.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Any pain in your groin as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.96,
      "end_seconds": 48.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "So, yes, for two weeks. As for pain in my groin, I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.3,
      "end_seconds": 54.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "what about not being able to stand, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.42,
      "end_seconds": 60.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "yeah. About a month, um, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.22,
      "end_seconds": 73.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "have you had any numbness or loss of consciousness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.49,
      "end_seconds": 81.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "So, I haven't had numbness or loss of consciousness, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.12,
      "end_seconds": 86.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Have you noticed head injury or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.0,
      "end_seconds": 91.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "So, no, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.99,
      "end_seconds": 96.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "On the the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.24,
      "end_seconds": 101.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "ah, no, that's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.91,
      "end_seconds": 107.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Okay, anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.23,
      "end_seconds": 111.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.95,
      "end_seconds": 129.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.11,
      "end_seconds": 133.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "no, I've never been operated on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.26,
      "end_seconds": 136.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.33,
      "end_seconds": 149.11,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "So, I had a reaction to erythromycin when I was younger, a rash, and I've avoided it since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.09,
      "end_seconds": 155.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.21,
      "end_seconds": 168.14,
      "duration_seconds": 11.93,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.92,
      "end_seconds": 173.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.91,
      "end_seconds": 186.54,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "um, I take alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week i take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 191.25,
      "end_seconds": 197.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the the last visit lists it as 25 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.07,
      "end_seconds": 203.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.93,
      "end_seconds": 213.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "No, I left it it at home. Erm, I was on spironolactone before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.04,
      "end_seconds": 216.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Right, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.43,
      "end_seconds": 220.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "yes, thin bones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.81,
      "end_seconds": 221.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.94,
      "end_seconds": 238.36,
      "duration_seconds": 15.42,
      "text": "Heart failure, for about ten years. I've been reading about it online and it worried me. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.76,
      "end_seconds": 240.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 241.63,
      "end_seconds": 258.94,
      "duration_seconds": 17.31,
      "text": "here are the numbers, doctor saturation 99 percent, pressure 125 over 74, temperature 36.6. Pulse is 67 beats a minute, respiratory rate 14, height 175 centimetres, weight 72 kilos, BMI works out to to 23.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.8,
      "end_seconds": 260.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.32,
      "end_seconds": 267.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.31,
      "end_seconds": 271.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Alright, does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.4,
      "end_seconds": 294.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "the left leg is shortened and turned outwards, and it is very painful to to move"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.53,
      "end_seconds": 301.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.99,
      "end_seconds": 351.57,
      "duration_seconds": 34.58,
      "text": "let me tell you where I've got to i'm honestly not certain yet it could be a probable hip fracture, or it might be a pelvic fracture i want blood tests done, that's for pre-operative that will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step i'd like to arrange an X-ray of the hip for hip fracture i'll start you on morphine, 2.5 milligrams, now, single dose that's for hip pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.19,
      "end_seconds": 362.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.42,
      "text": "Lie still, I am arranging an ambulance and pain relief. I'd like you to see the orthopaedic team as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.32,
      "end_seconds": 365.02,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.42,
      "end_seconds": 377.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.82,
      "end_seconds": 383.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "I mean, okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.24,
      "end_seconds": 390.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Let's review you straight away. So, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.57,
      "end_seconds": 395.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "okay, so thank you, doctor, goodbye"
    }
  ]
}